version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-09-29

abstract: >-
  Software for automated qualification and refinement of labelled training
  samples used in satellite image time series (SITS) classification,
  particularly for remote-sensing applications involving agricultural
  mapping and land-use and land-cover mapping. The software implements an
  integrated workflow comprising data preparation and standardization,
  automated hyperparameter selection for Self-Organizing Maps (SOMs),
  neural-network training, clustering of neurons into homogeneous
  spectro-temporal regions, and assessment of sample-label consistency.
  A Bayes-inspired heuristic based on empirical evidence is used to identify
  and remove potentially noisy or incorrectly labelled observations,
  producing refined training datasets. The software is implemented in Python
  and exposes its functionality through a REST programming interface,
  supporting parameterized and reproducible execution of the processing
  workflow.

